From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matteo Geromin <geromin.matteo@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: am335x-bbb-printer: disable I2C2

The bit-banged SPI bus uses the I2C2 pins (uart1_ctsn/uart1_rtsn) as
chip selects SPI0_CS2/SPI0_CS1. With I2C2 enabled by
am335x-bone-common.dtsi, spi_gpio failed to get its pins:

  pin PIN95 already requested by 4819c000.i2c; cannot claim for spi_gpio

and the touchscreen and stepper driver SPI devices were missing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/am335x-bbb-printer.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/am335x-bbb-printer.dts
index 1881bd2..f9412f6 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/am335x-bbb-printer.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/am335x-bbb-printer.dts
@@ -297,6 +297,15 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * The I2C2 pins (uart1_ctsn/uart1_rtsn, P9_20/P9_19) are the SPI0_CS2 and
+ * SPI0_CS1 chip selects of the bit-banged SPI bus (spi0_pins). Disable the
+ * BeagleBone I2C2 bus (cape EEPROMs) enabled by am335x-bone-common.dtsi.
+ */
+&i2c2 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 &tscadc {
 	status = "okay";
 };
